# And CGE can evolve the WebMCP interface itself

This is one of the coolest implications.

A WebMCP implementation isn't just:

> on / off.

It has design parameters:

```text
tool names
descriptions
input schemas
output structures
tool granularity
workflow decomposition
annotations
batching
error messages
state exposure
```

The WebMCP community is already discussing persistent tools surviving page navigation, reactive state updates instead of polling, and bulk/code-mode execution to reduce round trips. ([GitHub][2])

So CGE can literally evolve:

```text
WebMCPInterfaceVersion v1
          ↓
Harbor evaluation
          ↓
tool confusion observed
          ↓
GEPA modifies:
names / descriptions / schemas
          ↓
v2
          ↓
same workers
same tasks
          ↓
+14% completion
-22% tokens
```

Now the **tool interface itself is a Git-native asset**.

That's new inventory.

