# WebMCP makes ground truth easier too

One of our hardest issues has been:

> How do you know the evaluator is right?

Browser interaction is often nasty because:

```text
click happened
```

doesn't necessarily mean:

```text
business action succeeded.
```

Structured tools give you cleaner observable transitions:

```text
reserve_table(...)
→ reservation_id

refund_order(...)
→ refund transaction

save_document(...)
→ document revision
```

Therefore a Harbor World around WebMCP can often inspect actual state.

```text
BEFORE:
order.status = paid

ACTION:
refundOrder(...)

AFTER:
order.status = refunded
payment.refund_id exists
```

That's T0/T1-quality ground truth rather than an LLM judging a screenshot.

That will matter a lot for robust Schools.

