# Browser automation doesn't disappear

WebMCP will not instantly make the entire web structured.

So you get a capability ladder:

```text
preferred:

native structured API
      ↓
remote MCP
      ↓
WebMCP
      ↓
semantic DOM
      ↓
browser automation
      ↓
vision/computer use
```

Browser Use remains important as the fallback layer for arbitrary sites. It currently supports both browser automation and MCP connectivity, while BrowserGym gives reproducible browser-agent benchmarks across WebArena, WebArenaVerified, VisualWebArena, WorkArena, AssistantBench and others. ([GitHub][3])

This becomes a Lab decision:

```text
Can structured interface solve it?
YES → use it.

NO → browser automation.

Can we economically create a reusable
structured integration?

YES → molt it into an asset.
```

