# Then A2A adds an entirely new economic surface

A2A 1.0 is now the released standard for independent agents to discover capabilities, communicate and manage collaborative tasks without exposing their internal memory/tools. It had backing from more than 150 organizations by April 2026. ([Linux Foundation][6])

This could matter enormously to Moltwork later.

Today a WorkerRun might select:

```text
tool
```

Tomorrow:

```text
specialist agent
```

Example:

```text
campaign researcher
      │
      ├── use internal Letta skill
      │
      ├── call paid evaluator
      │
      ├── use WebMCP site
      │
      └── subcontract specialist agent over A2A
```

Now the resource-selection problem becomes:

```text
DO IT MYSELF
vs
USE A TOOL
vs
HIRE AN AGENT
vs
BUY AN ASSET
```

That's almost exactly the economic router Moltwork has been circling around.

