# UCP/ACP mean commerce itself is becoming agent-addressable

Google launched **Universal Commerce Protocol** in January 2026 with Shopify, Etsy, Target, Walmart, Wayfair and others. It's intended to cover discovery through checkout and post-purchase support and can integrate over APIs, MCP or A2A. ([Google Blog][7])

OpenAI and Stripe's **Agentic Commerce Protocol** similarly exposes seller checkout flows to compatible applications and can be implemented via REST or MCP. ([OpenAI][8])

So we should add another ontology axis:

```text
transaction_surface:
  manual
  HTTP
  x402-like micropayment
  ACP
  UCP
```

Moltwork doesn't need to win protocol wars.

It just needs to know:

> **This opportunity is machine-executable now.**

